    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, if the logs show the package was handled correctly/undamaged during shipping, why are we calling it an \"exception\"? Shouldn't we be more careful about approving these? I'm worried that if we just give in and call it an exception, we're basically teaching customers they can claim anything and we'll pay up. Can you look closer at the logs and tell me if there's any chance we can prove the customer is mistaken before we move forward with the credit?",
